{
  "name": "evdev",
  "description": "A comprehensive Rust implementation of the Linux evdev input subsystem interface, providing high-level abstractions for reading hardware events and managing device state. It features a synchronization engine to handle kernel ring buffer overflows (SYN_DROPPED) by injecting synthetic state updates, ensuring userspace state consistency. The library supports both physical device interaction and virtual device emulation via uinput, with optional asynchronous stream support through Tokio.",
